{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00049",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.37,
      "end_seconds": 6.18,
      "duration_seconds": 4.81,
      "text": "hello? Doctor? They told me to come straight in"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.01,
      "end_seconds": 11.24,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "not at all, please sit. What's the problem?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 13.04,
      "end_seconds": 26.31,
      "duration_seconds": 13.27,
      "text": "mainly pain low in the pelvis. There's a couple of other things, but that's the main one. I wasn't sure whether to come in at all, to be honest"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 27.87,
      "end_seconds": 30.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "How long are we talking about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 31.72,
      "end_seconds": 34.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "For two months, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 35.56,
      "end_seconds": 45.37,
      "duration_seconds": 9.81,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 46.69,
      "end_seconds": 53.22,
      "duration_seconds": 6.53,
      "text": "Okay, so it happens once or twice a day. It's moderate, honestly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 63.19,
      "end_seconds": 67.36,
      "duration_seconds": 4.17,
      "text": "alright, first the numbers, if you don't mind"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 73.92,
      "end_seconds": 75.61,
      "duration_seconds": 1.69,
      "text": "hold still for me.."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 90.39,
      "end_seconds": 97.86,
      "duration_seconds": 7.47,
      "text": "Okay: pressure 108 over 74, temperature 36.6. And heart rate 69, respiratory rate 18, saturation 99 percent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 99.22,
      "end_seconds": 103.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.85,
      "text": "Come over here and I'll have a look."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 107.02,
      "end_seconds": 107.72,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 108.57,
      "end_seconds": 110.52,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "Let me press here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 124.38,
      "end_seconds": 129.44,
      "duration_seconds": 5.06,
      "text": "There's tenderness in the lower tummy on the left, and no guarding."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 134.71,
      "end_seconds": 136.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.02,
      "text": "Good, that's the examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 147.84,
      "end_seconds": 151.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.96,
      "text": "Any vomiting, fever or bleeding between periods at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 152.96,
      "end_seconds": 157.85,
      "duration_seconds": 4.89,
      "text": "I haven't had vomiting, fever or bleeding between periods, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 158.27,
      "end_seconds": 162.79,
      "duration_seconds": 4.52,
      "text": "Okay, so. Any pins and needles or loss of strength anywhere?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 164.38,
      "end_seconds": 166.76,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "No, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 167.7,
      "end_seconds": 170.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "Before I prescribe anything, any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 171.14,
      "end_seconds": 176.77,
      "duration_seconds": 5.63,
      "text": "I mean, I'm allergic to to peanuts, I get hives."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 178.4,
      "end_seconds": 180.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "Anything special about your diet?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 182.22,
      "end_seconds": 185.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.69,
      "text": "I try to avoid too much sugar."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 188.47,
      "end_seconds": 190.75,
      "duration_seconds": 2.28,
      "text": "Do you get any exercise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 192.45,
      "end_seconds": 196.97,
      "duration_seconds": 4.52,
      "text": "I walk for about half an hour most days"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 205.58,
      "end_seconds": 208.24,
      "duration_seconds": 2.66,
      "text": "Have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 209.54,
      "end_seconds": 212.18,
      "duration_seconds": 2.64,
      "text": "No, never had any surgery."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 213.43,
      "end_seconds": 216.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.66,
      "text": "Any diagnoses you've been given before?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 218.13,
      "end_seconds": 227.25,
      "duration_seconds": 9.12,
      "text": "An underactive thyroid, for nearly five years. I did try to ignore it for a while."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 228.09,
      "end_seconds": 230.5,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "Does anything run in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 235.98,
      "end_seconds": 238.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "my father had kidney stones"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 239.82,
      "end_seconds": 243.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "Are you on any tablets or medication?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 244.57,
      "end_seconds": 248.96,
      "duration_seconds": 4.39,
      "text": "Thyronorm, 50 micrograms, every morning for my thyroid."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 250.96,
      "end_seconds": 259.18,
      "duration_seconds": 8.22,
      "text": "From what you've told me and what I found, this looks most like chronic pelvic pain, possibly endometriosis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 261.25,
      "end_seconds": 266.35,
      "duration_seconds": 5.1,
      "text": "I've been thinking the worst, to be honest. Is it bad?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 268.28,
      "end_seconds": 277.49,
      "duration_seconds": 9.21,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to to an emergency. It looks like chronic pelvic pain, possibly endometriosis, but I'd like to confirm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 295.72,
      "end_seconds": 321.33,
      "duration_seconds": 25.61,
      "text": "I think a pregnancy test makes sense here, for pelvic pain. The treatment will be mefenamic acid, 500 milligrams, three times a day with food, for five days. You take it by mouth. It's for period pain. A heat pad and some gentle movement help many people, and a pain diary helps me see a pattern."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 321.59,
      "end_seconds": 334.63,
      "duration_seconds": 13.04,
      "text": "Okay, so. If the pain becomes sudden and severe or you faint, or you feel really unwell, please come to the emergency department. Ask me anything before you go."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 338.58,
      "end_seconds": 343.22,
      "duration_seconds": 4.64,
      "text": "No, I think that's everything. Thank you, doctor."
    }
  ]
}